---
description: Pure helpers that do not use instance state belong in an anonymous namespace or as static members
globs: **/*.{h,hpp,cpp}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Pure helpers are static or file-local

A function that never uses `this` is not an instance method. `const` does not apply: there is no object to promise not to mutate. Leaving it as a non-static member implies hidden instance state and enlarges the class.

- Used only in one `.cpp`: put it in the **anonymous namespace** (internal linkage, off the class). Prefer this over `static` at namespace scope.
- Needed from multiple translation units, or as part of the type's API: declare it `static` on the class.
- Do not put a namespace-scope `static` function in a header (each TU would get its own copy).
- A file-local helper that owns **mutable** process-lifetime data (`static QHash`, `bool loaded`) is not “pure”. Colocate a mutex with that data (`shared-static-state.mdc`).

```cpp
// BAD — still on the class; looks like it can touch members
class TeamColorPicker {
  static QString colorToHex(const QColor& color);
  static QString normalizeHex(const QString& text);
};

// GOOD — file-local, next to other palette helpers
namespace {
QString colorToHex(const QColor& color);
QString normalizeHex(const QString& text);
}
```
